  "notes": "The anamnesis: the offering made in memory of the Passion, Resurrection and Ascension. MÉMORES at w003 governs the three genitives (passiónis, resurrectiónis, ascensiónis), the first of them seventeen words away — a long reach, though the corpus's longest is the Communicántes chain. FÍLII at w015 is the genitive singular the chain requires — eiúsdem Christi Fílii tui, Dómini nostri, four genitives in apposition — and Collatinus reads it so. Whitaker's carries filius with the contracted genitive only and so offers a plural or a locative; that is his entry's own coding, not a rule about -ius nouns, and the overruling is recorded in the pipeline's rulings. DATIS at w042 is tagged as the noun datum, with both analyzers, rather than as a participle of do. ÍNFERIS at w026 is the plural noun ínferi, those below; the phrase ab ínferis is the descéndit ad ínferos of the Apostles' Creed — a text this corpus does not carry — seen from the other side. CÆLOS at w031 is the masculine plural of cælum, neuter in its singular, which the lexicon carries. Witness do capitalises Hóstiam in the threefold naming of the victim; the edition prints it lowercase with witness handmissal-eo, adjudicated in the apparatus.",
